chx:X_SynthesisPackage a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SynthesisPackage ; rdfs:label "import pyttsx3"@en ; skos:definition "pyttsx3 is a third-party package, installed with pip install pyttsx3, that does not synthesise the voice itself but drives the speech engine that the operating system already has; its name is py for Python, tts for text-to-speech, x for extended and 3 for Python 3."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_PlatformEngines a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PlatformEngines ; rdfs:label "pyttsx3.init('dummy')"@en ; skos:definition "The engine behind pyttsx3 depends on the platform: SAPI5 on Windows, NSSpeechSynthesizer on macOS and eSpeak on Linux; the package lists the engines per platform with the first as the default, and also ships a dummy driver that speaks nothing and is meant for tests."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_PlatformEngines a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "{'win32': 'sapi5', 'darwin': 'nsss'}.get('linux', 'espeak') evaluates to 'espeak'"@en ; chx:input "{'win32': 'sapi5', 'darwin': 'nsss'}.get('linux', 'espeak')" ; chx:output "'espeak'" .
chx:X_PlatformEngines rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_PlatformEngines .
chx:X_InitFunction a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:InitFunction ; rdfs:label "engine = pyttsx3.init()"@en ; skos:definition "pyttsx3.init() returns an Engine object for a named driver or the platform default and returns the same object again for the same driver while it is alive; when the driver cannot start, as with eSpeak missing on Linux, it raises RuntimeError."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_SayMethod a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SayMethod ; rdfs:label "engine.say('Hello.')"@en ; skos:definition "say() adds a text to the engine's queue and returns at once; it does not speak, and it returns an error message instead of queuing when the text is empty or only spaces."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_RunAndWait a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RunAndWait ; rdfs:label "engine.runAndWait()"@en ; skos:definition "runAndWait() starts the engine, works through everything queued so far and blocks until the last utterance is finished; without it nothing queued by say(), setProperty() or save_to_file() takes effect."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_EngineEvents a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:EngineEvents ; rdfs:label "engine.connect('finished-utterance', callback)"@en ; skos:definition "connect() registers a callback for one of the engine's events: started-utterance, started-word, finished-utterance or error; the callbacks run during runAndWait(), and each receives the name given to say()."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_SpeakShortcut a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SpeakShortcut ; rdfs:label "pyttsx3.speak('Hello.')"@en ; skos:definition "Version 2.99 has a module-level speak(text) that gets the engine with init(), queues the text with say() and calls runAndWait(), which the chapter does not show."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_GetProperty a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GetProperty ; rdfs:label "engine.getProperty('rate')"@en ; skos:definition "getProperty() reads a setting by name: 'rate' is words per minute, 'volume' a float from 0.0 to 1.0, 'voice' the current voice and 'voices' the plural list of all Voice objects; an unknown name raises KeyError."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_SetProperty a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SetProperty ; rdfs:label "engine.setProperty('rate', 300)"@en ; skos:definition "setProperty() queues a change of 'rate', 'volume' or 'voice'; the singular 'voice' takes the id of a Voice, and like speech the change is applied only when runAndWait() runs the queue."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_SpeechRate a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SpeechRate ; rdfs:label "60 / 200"@en ; skos:definition "The rate is the speaking speed in words per minute and starts at 200, so at the default each word takes on average 60 / 200 of a second."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_SpeechRate a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "60 / 200 evaluates to 0.3"@en ; chx:input "60 / 200" ; chx:output "0.3" .
chx:X_SpeechRate rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SpeechRate .
chx:X_VoiceObjects a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:VoiceObjects ; rdfs:label "engine.getProperty('voices')"@en ; skos:definition "A Voice object has the attributes id, name, languages, gender and age; gender and age are None and languages is an empty list when the operating system does not say, and a list of Voice objects prints as <pyttsx3.voice.Voice object at 0x...> because the class defines no repr."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_SaveToFile a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SaveToFile ; rdfs:label "engine.save_to_file('Hello.', 'hello.wav')"@en ; skos:definition "save_to_file() queues speech to be written to a file instead of the speakers, and like say() it needs runAndWait() before the file exists; the chapter says that only .wav is possible, which is true of the eSpeak and SAPI5 drivers and not of the macOS driver, which writes .aiff."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_WavContainer a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:WavContainer ; rdfs:label "wave.open('hello.wav', 'rb')"@en ; skos:definition "A WAV file is a RIFF container holding a format header and raw samples; the standard wave module reads and writes it, and the eSpeak driver of pyttsx3 writes mono, 2-byte samples at 22,050 frames per second, so one second of silence is 44 header bytes plus 44,100 data bytes."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_WavContainer a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(lambda io, wave: (lambda b: (lambda w: (w.setnchannels(1), w.setsampwidth(2), w.setframerate(22050), w.writeframes(bytes(44100)), w.close(), (b.getvalue()[:4], b.getvalue()[8:12], len(b.getvalue())))[-1])(wave.open(b, 'wb')))(io.BytesIO()))(__import__('io'), __import__('wave')) evaluates to (b'RIFF', b'WAVE', 44144)"@en ; chx:input "(lambda io, wave: (lambda b: (lambda w: (w.setnchannels(1), w.setsampwidth(2), w.setframerate(22050), w.writeframes(bytes(44100)), w.close(), (b.getvalue()[:4], b.getvalue()[8:12], len(b.getvalue())))[-1])(wave.open(b, 'wb')))(io.BytesIO()))(__import__('io'), __import__('wave'))" ; chx:output "(b'RIFF', b'WAVE', 44144)" .
chx:X_WavContainer rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_WavContainer .
chx:X_SpeechDuration a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SpeechDuration ; rdfs:label "1800 / 200"@en ; skos:definition "The length of speech follows from the word count and the rate: 1,800 words at 200 words per minute take 9 minutes, which agrees in size with the 10-minute file that the chapter reports for its laptop."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_SpeechDuration a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "1800 / 200 evaluates to 9.0"@en ; chx:input "1800 / 200" ; chx:output "9.0" .
chx:X_SpeechDuration rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SpeechDuration .
chx:X_RemovedAudioModules a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RemovedAudioModules ; rdfs:label "import wave"@en ; skos:definition "Python 3.13 removed aifc, audioop, sunau, chunk and sndhdr from the standard library under PEP 594 and kept wave; under 3.14.4 only wave can still be imported, so AIFF files, which the macOS driver of pyttsx3 writes, need a third-party reader."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_WhisperPackage a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:WhisperPackage ; rdfs:label "pip install openai-whisper"@en ; skos:definition "Whisper is installed as openai-whisper, because the package called whisper on PyPI is something else; it depends on PyTorch and other large packages and needs the ffmpeg program on the path, which the chapter does not mention; this was read and not installed here."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_LoadModel a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:LoadModel ; rdfs:label "model = whisper.load_model('base')"@en ; skos:definition "load_model(name) returns a model object; release 20250625 accepts fourteen names, among them the chapter's tiny, base, small, medium and large-v3, the .en models for English only, large-v1, large-v2, large, and turbo; the first call downloads the model file."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_ModelSizes a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ModelSizes ; rdfs:label "whisper.load_model('large-v3')"@en ; skos:definition "Larger models are slower and more accurate: on the chapter's 15-minute sample the author's laptop needed 2 minutes 34 seconds for base and 32 minutes 58 seconds for large-v3, about 12.8 times as long; these times are the book's own measurements, not reproduced here."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_ModelSizes a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "round((32 * 60 + 58) / (2 * 60 + 34), 1) evaluates to 12.8"@en ; chx:input "round((32 * 60 + 58) / (2 * 60 + 34), 1)" ; chx:output "12.8" .
chx:X_ModelSizes rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ModelSizes .
chx:X_GraphicsProcessor a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GraphicsProcessor ; rdfs:label "whisper.load_model('base', device='cuda')"@en ; skos:definition "By default Whisper computes on the CPU; with an NVIDIA card and the matching PyTorch the device argument 'cuda' moves the model to the graphics processor and speeds transcription up; this was read and not run here."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_TranscribeMethod a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TranscribeMethod ; rdfs:label "result = model.transcribe('hello.wav')"@en ; skos:definition "transcribe(path) decodes the audio or video file and returns a dictionary; it can take seconds or hours depending on the model and the length, and it accepts a language argument; it was read and not run here."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_ResultDictionary a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ResultDictionary ; rdfs:label "result['text']"@en ; skos:definition "The dictionary returned by transcribe() has the keys text, segments and language; the 'text' value is the whole transcription and every entry of 'segments' has start and end in seconds and its own text."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_ResultDictionary a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "{'text': ' Hello. How are you doing?', 'segments': [{'start': 0.0, 'end': 2.5, 'text': ' Hello. How are you doing?'}], 'language': 'en'}['text'].strip() evaluates to 'Hello. How are you doing?'"@en ; chx:input "{'text': ' Hello. How are you doing?', 'segments': [{'start': 0.0, 'end': 2.5, 'text': ' Hello. How are you doing?'}], 'language': 'en'}['text'].strip()" ; chx:output "'Hello. How are you doing?'" .
chx:X_ResultDictionary rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ResultDictionary .
chx:X_LanguageOption a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:LanguageOption ; rdfs:label "model.transcribe('hello.wav', language='English')"@en ; skos:definition "Without a language argument Whisper detects the language from the first 30 seconds; with one it skips that step, and the name may be a code such as 'en' or a name such as 'English', which is lower-cased; the package knows 100 languages."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_AudioDecoding a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:AudioDecoding ; rdfs:label "ffmpeg -i hello.wav -f s16le -ac 1 -ar 16000 -"@en ; skos:definition "Whisper does not read the file itself: it starts ffmpeg to convert any audio or video file to 16,000 samples per second of mono 16-bit sound, and it processes that sound in 30-second chunks of 480,000 samples."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_AudioDecoding a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "30 * 16000 evaluates to 480000"@en ; chx:input "30 * 16000" ; chx:output "480000" .
chx:X_AudioDecoding rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_AudioDecoding .
chx:X_HumanReview a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HumanReview ; rdfs:label "print(result['text'])"@en ; skos:definition "All models make errors, including in punctuation and capital letters, so the chapter asks that a person review every transcription and suggests trying a larger model when there are many errors."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_SrtFormat a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SrtFormat ; rdfs:label "00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,640"@en ; skos:definition "A SubRip file holds numbered blocks separated by a blank line, each with a start and end time as hours:minutes:seconds,milliseconds with a comma and then the text; Whisper's SRT writer always writes the hours."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_SrtFormat a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(lambda ms: '%02d:%02d:%02d,%03d' % (ms // 3600000, ms % 3600000 // 60000, ms % 60000 // 1000, ms % 1000))(round(5.64 * 1000)) evaluates to '00:00:05,640'"@en ; chx:input "(lambda ms: '%02d:%02d:%02d,%03d' % (ms // 3600000, ms % 3600000 // 60000, ms % 60000 // 1000, ms % 1000))(round(5.64 * 1000))" ; chx:output "'00:00:05,640'" .
chx:X_SrtFormat rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SrtFormat .
chx:X_VttFormat a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:VttFormat ; rdfs:label "00:05.640"@en ; skos:definition "A WebVTT file starts with the line WEBVTT and writes times with a full stop before the milliseconds; the hours may be left out when they are zero, which is how Whisper writes them."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_VttFormat a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(lambda ms: '%02d:%02d.%03d' % (ms % 3600000 // 60000, ms % 60000 // 1000, ms % 1000))(round(5.64 * 1000)) evaluates to '00:05.640'"@en ; chx:input "(lambda ms: '%02d:%02d.%03d' % (ms % 3600000 // 60000, ms % 60000 // 1000, ms % 1000))(round(5.64 * 1000))" ; chx:output "'00:05.640'" .
chx:X_VttFormat rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_VttFormat .
chx:X_TsvFormat a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TsvFormat ; rdfs:label "start end text"@en ; skos:definition "Whisper's TSV file is not an official subtitle format: it has the header line start, end and text separated by tabs and then one line per segment with the times as integer milliseconds, which any program with the csv module can read."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_TsvFormat a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(round(1000 * 5.64), round(1000 * 14.96)) evaluates to (5640, 14960)"@en ; chx:input "(round(1000 * 5.64), round(1000 * 14.96))" ; chx:output "(5640, 14960)" .
chx:X_TsvFormat rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TsvFormat .
chx:X_TxtAndJsonFormats a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TxtAndJsonFormats ; rdfs:label "get_writer('json', '.')"@en ; skos:definition "The TXT writer writes one stripped segment text per line and the JSON writer dumps the whole result dictionary with json.dump; the chapter lists both names in the get_writer() argument."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_TxtAndJsonFormats a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "__import__('json').dumps({'start': 0, 'end': 1.5, 'text': ' a'}) evaluates to '{'start': 0, 'end': 1.5, 'text': ' a'}'"@en ; chx:input "__import__('json').dumps({'start': 0, 'end': 1.5, 'text': ' a'})" ; chx:output "'{'start': 0, 'end': 1.5, 'text': ' a'}'" .
chx:X_TxtAndJsonFormats rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TxtAndJsonFormats .
chx:X_GetWriter a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GetWriter ; rdfs:label "whisper.utils.get_writer('srt', '.')"@en ; skos:definition "get_writer(format, folder) returns a writer function, and calling it with the result and an audio file name writes folder/name.format, where the name is the audio file's name without its folder and extension; an unknown format raises KeyError."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_GetWriter a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "__import__('os').path.splitext(__import__('os').path.basename('talks/hello.wav'))[0] + '.srt' evaluates to 'hello.srt'"@en ; chx:input "__import__('os').path.splitext(__import__('os').path.basename('talks/hello.wav'))[0] + '.srt'" ; chx:output "'hello.srt'" .
chx:X_GetWriter rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GetWriter .
chx:X_WordTimestamps a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:WordTimestamps ; rdfs:label "write_function(result, 'audio', {'max_words_per_line': 2})"@en ; skos:definition "When the transcription was made with word timestamps, every segment also holds a list of words with their own times, and the writer can then start a new subtitle after a number of words or a line width; the chapter does not cover these options."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_YtDlpPackage a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:YtDlpPackage ; rdfs:label "import yt_dlp"@en ; skos:definition "yt-dlp is a third-party package that downloads from YouTube and many other video sites; it is installed with pip, changes often as the sites change, and the chapter's first advice for an error is to install the latest version; it was run here only offline, in a scratch environment."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_DownloadCall a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DownloadCall ; rdfs:label "ydl.download([video_url])"@en ; skos:definition "download() is called with a list of addresses inside a with yt_dlp.YoutubeDL() block; current yt-dlp also accepts one address, wrapping it in a list itself; the download needs a network and was not run."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_DownloadOptions a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DownloadOptions ; rdfs:label "yt_dlp.YoutubeDL({'quiet': True})"@en ; skos:definition "The dictionary given to YoutubeDL holds options such as quiet and no_warnings to silence the output, outtmpl for the file name, format for the choice of stream, postprocessors for steps after the download, and skip_download to fetch only information."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_OutputTemplate a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:OutputTemplate ; rdfs:label "'outtmpl': 'downloaded_content.%(ext)s'"@en ; skos:definition "The outtmpl option is an output template: the text is filled in with printf-style named fields, so %(ext)s becomes the real file extension and the script can know the file's stem in advance; without it the name is built from the video's title and id."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_OutputTemplate a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "'downloaded_content.%(ext)s' % {'ext': 'm4a'} evaluates to 'downloaded_content.m4a'"@en ; chx:input "'downloaded_content.%(ext)s' % {'ext': 'm4a'}" ; chx:output "'downloaded_content.m4a'" .
chx:X_OutputTemplate rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_OutputTemplate .
chx:X_AudioExtraction a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:AudioExtraction ; rdfs:label "'format': 'm4a/bestaudio/best'"@en ; skos:definition "The format option lists choices separated by slashes, tried from left to right, and the FFmpegExtractAudio post-processor then extracts the sound with ffmpeg into the preferred codec; it needs ffmpeg installed and a network, and was not run."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_AudioExtraction a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "'m4a/bestaudio/best'.split('/') evaluates to ['m4a', 'bestaudio', 'best']"@en ; chx:input "'m4a/bestaudio/best'.split('/')" ; chx:output "['m4a', 'bestaudio', 'best']" .
chx:X_AudioExtraction rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_AudioExtraction .
chx:X_FindDownloadedFile a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:FindDownloadedFile ; rdfs:label "Path().glob('downloaded_content.*')"@en ; skos:definition "Because the extension can vary, the script finds the file with a glob pattern: Path().glob('downloaded_content.*') yields every file in the current folder whose name is downloaded_content followed by any extension, and the chapter takes the first."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_FindDownloadedFile a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(__import__('pathlib').PurePath('downloaded_content.m4a').match('downloaded_content.*'), __import__('pathlib').PurePath('notes.txt').match('downloaded_content.*')) evaluates to (True, False)"@en ; chx:input "(__import__('pathlib').PurePath('downloaded_content.m4a').match('downloaded_content.*'), __import__('pathlib').PurePath('notes.txt').match('downloaded_content.*'))" ; chx:output "(True, False)" .
chx:X_FindDownloadedFile rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_FindDownloadedFile .
chx:X_MetadataOnly a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MetadataOnly ; rdfs:label "ydl.extract_info(video_url)"@en ; skos:definition "With skip_download set, extract_info() returns a dictionary of facts about the video, such as title and duration; sanitize_info() turns that dictionary into something JSON can store, and the chapter writes it to metadata.json with json.dumps and encoding utf-8."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_MetadataOnly a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "__import__('json').loads(__import__('json').dumps({'title': 'T', 'duration': 60}))['duration'] evaluates to 60"@en ; chx:input "__import__('json').loads(__import__('json').dumps({'title': 'T', 'duration': 60}))['duration']" ; chx:output "60" .
chx:X_MetadataOnly rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MetadataOnly .
chx:X_FilenameCleaning a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:FilenameCleaning ; rdfs:label "yt_dlp.YoutubeDL({}).prepare_filename(info)"@en ; skos:definition "The chapter says characters not allowed in filenames are excluded from a title-based name; yt-dlp 2026.8.19 instead replaces them with look-alike characters, so 'What: is? this/that' becomes a name with a full-width colon, a full-width question mark and a division-like slash, followed by the id in square brackets."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_DownloadFailures a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DownloadFailures ; rdfs:label "pip install --upgrade yt-dlp"@en ; skos:definition "A site may refuse a download because of age or login rules, location or protection against scripts; the chapter's first step is to update yt-dlp, which follows the sites' changes, and a script should treat a failed download as a normal outcome."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_PracticeQuestions a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PracticeQuestions ; rdfs:label "Practice questions 1 to 7"@en ; skos:definition "The seven practice questions ask: how to make pyttsx3 speak faster (raise the 'rate' property), which format it saves (WAV, with the exceptions above), whether pyttsx3 and Whisper need online services (no, apart from Whisper's first model download), whether they support other languages (yes), which model is the default (the chapter recommends base but does not call it a default, while the command line of release 20250625 uses turbo), which two subtitle formats are common (SRT and VTT), and whether yt-dlp works on other sites than YouTube (yes)."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:X_GuessWithVoice a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GuessWithVoice ; rdfs:label "speak('Your guess, 42, is too low.')"@en ; skos:definition "The first practice program replaces print() in the guess-the-number game by a function speak() that prints the text and also says it, and makes the hints name the guess, such as Your guess, 42, is too low."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_GuessWithVoice a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "(lambda guess, secret: 'Your guess, %d, is too %s.' % (guess, 'low' if guess < secret else 'high'))(42, 50) evaluates to 'Your guess, 42, is too low.'"@en ; chx:input "(lambda guess, secret: 'Your guess, %d, is too %s.' % (guess, 'low' if guess < secret else 'high'))(42, 50)" ; chx:output "'Your guess, 42, is too low.'" .
chx:X_GuessWithVoice rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GuessWithVoice .
chx:X_BottlesSong a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BottlesSong ; rdfs:label "'%d bottle%s' % (n, ...)"@en ; skos:definition "The second practice program speaks 99 Bottles of Beer, each verse one bottle fewer, down to the line No more bottles of beer on the wall; starting at 2 or 3 makes testing easier, and the word bottle needs its singular form for one bottle."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:IO_BottlesSong a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "[('1 bottle' if n == 1 else '%d bottles' % n) for n in (2, 1, 0)] evaluates to ['2 bottles', '1 bottle', '0 bottles']"@en ; chx:input "[('1 bottle' if n == 1 else '%d bottles' % n) for n in (2, 1, 0)]" ; chx:output "['2 bottles', '1 bottle', '0 bottles']" .
chx:X_BottlesSong rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BottlesSong .
chx:X_TranscriberGlue a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TranscriberGlue ; rdfs:label "transcribe_all(urls, download, transcribe, write)"@en ; skos:definition "The third practice program glues yt-dlp and Whisper: for each address it downloads the audio, transcribes it and writes an SRT file; passing the three steps in as functions lets the loop be tested offline with stand-ins, while the real steps need a network and a model."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:Artifact a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:DomainOntologyArtifact ; rdfs:label "SEN0414 chapter 24 domain ontology"@en ;
    rd:derivedFromResearchSubject <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> ; rd:hasCompetencyQuestion chx:CQs ; rd:hasSourceProvenance chx:Provenance ;
    rd:hasReusabilityScope rd:RS_SubjectSpecific ; rd:hasResolutionEnvironment chx:Env .
chx:CQs a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:CompetencyQuestionSet ; rdfs:label "Chapter 24 competency questions"@en ; rd:containsCompetencyQuestion chx:CQ1, chx:CQ2 .
chx:CQ1 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:CompetencyQuestion ; rdfs:label "Which parts of the chapter's speech programs run without a sound card, a speech model, a download or a network, and which cannot?"@en .
chx:CQ2 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:CompetencyQuestion ; rdfs:label "Where do the chapter's statements about file formats, model names and package behaviour differ from the current package sources, and on what source?"@en .
chx:Provenance a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:ResearchSubjectInput ; rdfs:label "Derived from the chapter 24 research artefact"@en ;
    skos:definition "Concepts are corpus-derived from the 3rd edition's chapter 24 through the Stage 1 research artefact; the modern-practice branch comes from that artefact's secondary sources."@en ;
    dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/research> .
chx:Env a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:ResolutionEnvironment ; rdfs:label "CPython 3.14.4"@en ;
    skos:definition "Every input-output example executed under CPython 3.14.4, installed with uv on 2026-10-01."@en ;
    dcterms:source "The execution run recorded with this build, 08-tooling/sen0414_rdodi_build_v1_1_0.py" .

